    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d104">

                <pb facs="0165" n="157" xml:id="pg157"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/7278: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-02-02T18:00:00-05:00">February 2, 1938—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>49. Your 79, January 31, 7 p.m. You may inform the Foreign Office that I shall
                    take an early opportunity to deplore on behalf of the American public recent
                    bombardments from the air of undefended and thickly populated cities.<anchor
                        n="15" xml:id="d104-f1"/> For your information, I think it wiser to make
                    such a statement complete in itself without relation to expressions on the same
                    subject by either the British or French Governments.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d104-f1" n="15" xml:id="d104-f1-content">
                <p>Similar instructions were sent to the Ambassador in France in telegram No. 59,
                    February 2, 6 p.m.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
